WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:03.095
Welcome to SysNDD.

00:03.229 --> 00:06.360
Today, let's look up a gene together.

00:06.867 --> 00:09.006
What does SysNDD grade, and how?

00:09.139 --> 00:12.236
Let's find out in three parts: the resource,

00:12.370 --> 00:17.507
the entity, and the four evidence categories.

00:18.033 --> 00:22.270
SysNDD is an expert-curated database of gene-disease

00:22.403 --> 00:26.105
associations in neurodevelopmental disorders, or NDDs.

00:26.238 --> 00:33.238
The home page names three uses:
clinical diagnostics, counseling, and research.

00:34.243 --> 00:40.337
Clinicians and scientists grade
the published evidence with consistent criteria.

00:40.867 --> 00:46.447
In the search box,
type a gene symbol, for example <i>FBXO11</i>.

00:46.580 --> 00:48.416
Then select the suggestion.

00:48.549 --> 00:49.964
The gene page opens.

00:50.098 --> 00:52.787
No account is needed.

00:53.300 --> 00:57.233
SysNDD grades entities, not genes.

00:57.366 --> 01:02.022
An entity is one gene,
one mode of inheritance and one disease.

01:02.155 --> 01:07.765
The gene has an identifier from HGNC,
the HUGO Gene Nomenclature Committee.

01:07.898 --> 01:12.089
The inheritance is a term
from the Human Phenotype Ontology.

01:12.223 --> 01:16.901
The disease has an identifier from OMIM or MONDO.

01:17.433 --> 01:22.824
On the gene page,
the Associated table lists two entities for <i>FBXO11</i>.

01:22.957 --> 01:29.299
Both have the same gene,
but the inheritance differs: autosomal dominant

01:29.432 --> 01:33.643
and autosomal recessive, and so does the disease.

01:33.777 --> 01:37.673
So each entity carries its own category.

01:38.200 --> 01:42.508
Below the table, cards show external data from gnomAD,

01:42.641 --> 01:46.188
the Genome Aggregation Database, and from ClinVar.

01:46.322 --> 01:49.111
They are context, not curation.

01:49.244 --> 01:56.121
A ClinVar classification rates a variant;
a SysNDD category rates an entity.

01:56.633 --> 02:02.153
Within the NDD scope,
every entity has one evidence category.

02:02.286 --> 02:07.360
Definitive means published,
with a clear-cut number of cases or families,

02:07.493 --> 02:10.280
or with several criteria that add up.

02:10.413 --> 02:15.883
Moderate means better evidence than Limited,
but not enough for Definitive.

02:16.017 --> 02:18.262
Limited means published,

02:18.396 --> 02:22.719
with intellectual disability
indicated, but limited evidence.

02:22.852 --> 02:27.686
Refuted means newer evidence
contradicts the association.

02:27.819 --> 02:34.819
Entities outside the NDD scope are
marked Not applicable: a tag, not a category.

02:35.967 --> 02:39.962
The autosomal dominant entity is Definitive.

02:40.095 --> 02:46.526
Its clinical synopsis summarizes
the affected individuals and their features.

02:47.033 --> 02:50.765
The autosomal recessive entity is Refuted.

02:50.899 --> 02:54.948
The synopsis explains why: in the one reported patient,

02:55.081 --> 03:00.059
a likely pathogenic variant
in a different gene was found later.

03:00.192 --> 03:06.073
A category grades the published
evidence; it is not a diagnosis.

03:06.600 --> 03:11.221
Remember: SysNDD grades entities, not genes.

03:11.355 --> 03:15.108
Each entity in the NDD scope has one category.

03:15.241 --> 03:19.419
So when you look up a gene, check all of its entities.

03:19.933 --> 03:26.572
The documentation chapter Find a gene
explains every part of these pages.
